commit 1cbe3dcf6bdbe94b0563bac10d4d5affe8099c04
Author: saadahmed95 <saad.ahmed95@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 1 16:14:54 2026 +0200

    fix(ws): answer one message per session at a time

    A user_message arriving while another was still streaming started a
    second orchestrator run on the same session: the runs interleaved
    their entries, both streamed to the socket, and the second handed the
    model the first answer half-written. The WS transport now queues each
    user_message on a PerSessionLock keyed by session id, so a session
    answers one message at a time, in arrival order. A ping and a frame
    that fails validation are still answered at once; a failed
    user_message's stream_end is queued, so stream_ends keep arrival
    order.

    Fixes #47

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

